# Agent Self-Evaluation (mandatory)

**Every agent turn that responds to the user MUST end with a `### Self-evaluation` block.** No exceptions — including read-only Q&A, single-line answers, Ask mode, and failed/aborted work.

Full process: `.cursor/skills/agent-self-evaluation/SKILL.md`

## Hard requirements

1. **Run before sending the final message** — not optional, not deferred to a follow-up.
2. **Include the handoff block** (≤6 lines) as the **last section** of the response.
3. **§6 skill feedback loop** — always ask whether a skill update would have prevented churn; edit skills in the same turn when yes; otherwise state `Skills updated: none`.
4. **Never skip** because the task was "trivial", "docs-only", "question-only", or "no code changed".

## Handoff block (required format)

```markdown
### Self-evaluation
- **Scope:** <on-target | read-only | note drift>
- **Tests:** <paths + result | n/a + why>
- **Skills used:** <names | none>
- **Skills updated:** <skill + one-line change | none>
- **Commit-ready:** <yes | no | n/a>
```

## Pair with agent-triage

Start every task with [agent-triage](../skills/agent-triage/SKILL.md). End every task with self-evaluation. A response without the handoff block is **incomplete**.
